{
 "schema": "aow.later/1",
 "_doc": "Beast anatomy, concept round BA1 (2026-10-30; Dominic, on centaur romans' war elephant in play: 'quality here is bad, they are clearly a bunch of spheres put together ... we need to improve'). The war elephant and the centaur's horse half sculpted in Blender, two looks each, for tests/sheets/beast_anatomy_ba1.json (nothing in the game loads this file). Elephant a (eastern: arched back, twin-domed forehead, small ears, short tusks), b (bush: high shoulder, sloping forehead, fan ears, long tusks): tools/blender/elephant.py, src/model/siege.lobster elephant(look). Centaur a (a riding horse's half), b (a heavy horse's, feathered fetlocks): tools/blender/centaur.py, src/model/units2.lobster body_centaur, hoof_leg_sculpted. Round BA2 (2026-10-30; Dominic on BA1: 'the elephant looks better mostly, weird ears. But the centaurs looks mad'): centaur c (a riding horse's half in a horse's proportions, the man standing up out of the breast), d (the same a size up), e (a heavy horse, feathered); the elephants' ears rebuilt hanging from the head (tools/blender/centaur.py; BA1's centaurs: centaur_ba1.py). Round BA3 (2026-10-31, after 'a banana with the human part perched on top'): body.pony_fused_f/_g, leg.hoof[_hind]_f/_g, creatures pony_ba3_f/_g (tools/blender/centaur.py; BA2 kept as centaur_ba2.py).",
